   {
    "name": "ambulance_agreement.txt",
    "text": "Halden Medical Transport\nBookings Office\n\n10 February 2027\n\nDear Helen Achterberg,\n\nThank you for your booking and payment. This letter is your agreement with us for ambulance cover at the Beacon Heritage Run 7K on 26 June 2027. One ambulance and two paramedics will be on site at the rowing club, in place by 07:00, and will stay until the race has finished. Booking reference EV-47207.\n\nOur crew leader will find your race director when they arrive.\n\nKind regards,\nRhys Morgan\nBookings Manager\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "insurance.txt",
    "text": "CERT OF INS.   REF EV-19794\nMeridian Mutual Insurance   POL NO EL-648959\nINSURED ....... Beacon Food Bank\nRISK LOCATION .. Stonebridge\nFROM .......... June 25, 2027\nTO ............ June 27, 2027\nINDEMNITY ..... $1,000,000\nACTIVITY ...... Foot race (Beacon Heritage Run 7K)\nISSUED ........ February 10, 2027\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "medical_plan.txt",
    "text": "Beacon Heritage Run 7K - medical notes\nSaturday 26 June 2027 / gun 08:30 / 150 runners / 7K\ncontact Helen Achterberg 555-0162\nAn ambulance from Halden Medical Transport is on site for the race; the paperwork is attached.\n\nFIRST AID\ncommittee members w/ work first aid certs. kit at HQ tent + kit in lead car\n\nWEATHER / WATER\nwater every 2.5k. forecast check -48h and -2h. >28C earlier start or shorter course. >32C cancel. foil + warm tent at finish if cold/wet\n\nHOSPITAL\nNorthshore District Hospital, 27km from finish. pickup point the rowing club, route walked w/ first aiders. ED told date + numbers\n\nCOMMS\nradios on medical channel at all posts + bikes, phones backup. amb calls go via medical lead, who gives crew the barrier to come to\n\nLEAD\nrace director + committee\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "race_plan.txt",
    "text": "RACE PLAN\nBeacon Heritage Run 7K | Saturday 26 June 2027\nOrganiser: Beacon Food Bank\nRace director: Helen Achterberg\nReference: AG-15988\n\nOverview\nThe Beacon Heritage Run 7K is a 7K race of 7 km for 150 entrants, based in the Stonebridge area of Port Halden. The start is at 08:30 and the course closes at 10:00.\n\nCourse\nThe course stays entirely on the Lakeshore Promenade and the Cathedral Green loop, away from the highway, and no road is closed for the race. The finish is at the boathouse.\n\nCourse dimensions\nThe Lakeshore Promenade is a promenade 7 m wide with open ground alongside. The Cathedral Green loop section runs across parkland, with a marked lane of 9 m and open grass on both sides. The start pens sit on the grass, side by side.\n\nSupport\nEntrants collect numbers from the rowing club from one hour before the start. Timing is by chip, with mats at the start and finish. Results are posted on the Beacon website the same day.\n"
   }
  ],
  "cover_letter": "Hello,\n\nI am writing on behalf of our organisation about this year's race.\n\nHere is our application for the Beacon Heritage Run 7K, Saturday 26 June 2027. 150 runners, 7K, off at 08:30, around Stonebridge. I've attached ambulance_agreement.txt, insurance.txt, medical_plan.txt, race_plan.txt.\n\nWe look forward to hearing from you.\n\nThanks,\nHelen\n\nHelen Achterberg, Beacon Food Bank\n555-0162\n",
